OK, I've played for a few hours, and I've discovered a few neat tricks that
can make your game more or less fun depending on whether you like abuses or
not.


If any of these has been posted before, then I don't take credit for it.


SPOILER!!!!!!! DO NOT READ FURTHER IF YOU DON'T LIKE SPOILERS!


1.  You can polymorph your pet into anything with the following items:

magical resistance item
magic whistle
speed boots

  Wearing the magical resistance item, step on a polymorph trap.  Blow
the magic whistle and summon your wimpy pet.  Then displace your pet,
and it will be forced onto the polymorph trap and made to polymorph.
If you get a demon of some type, just keep trying and eventually it will
fail its saving throw and be polymorphed into something else.  Minotaurs
and Olog-hai's are especially effective.  For some reason, mumakils are
weak.

With a powerful pet, it's easy to deal with humans you shouldn't kill
like shopkeepers and temple priests.  I don't know if killing Croesus
loses your telepathy intrinsic.


2.  Get a few create monster wands off some monsters (many carry them).
Now sit by an altar and start zapping the wand and sacrificing corpses.
Some of the summoned monsters will be carrying more wands, and thus you
can have a good run of monsters before the wands run out.


3.  Polypiling still works, though to some lessened capacity, I'd bet.

4.  The four artifacts I've gotten are:  Sting, Magicbane (N-athame),
Vorpal Blade (N-blade?), and Mjollnir.  BTW, I can wield Mjolly even
though it's a good alignment weapon.

5.  At the bottom of the gnome caverns, there is a hidden room with a
luckstone in it.

6.  In one of the magic memory vaults, there is a portal to Croesus's
castle, where a million annoying wimpy soldiers await their death.  In
that castle, there is ~ 50K gold and some valuable gems.  There is also
a David's treasure zoo there, but everything on the level is woken up
by an alarm, so be prepared to fight forever.

7.  THe only way I've found to rob the shopkeeper is to steal something,
lure him to some branch-point you've already trashed through, and then
leave him there.  I had to get some stuff from a shop on the 8th level,
so I stole something small, waded through some Kops, and waited by the
stairs until that fool of a shopkeeper got next to me.  Then I ran up
stairs and got away to heal (You need some good speed to do this).  Then
I kept doing this until I got to the balance castle portal and lured him
in.  I left him behind, and he never came back.  However, this takes
good armor, good speed, and good HP's, but you'll never have to kill
him and lose your telepathy.

That's all for now.  So long



